a las vegas man's desperate plea to help  his wife and child evacuate afghanistan  thank you for joining us tonight at five  o'clock i'm sasha loftis though  thousands were able to leave with the  help of u.s troops the sad reality is  many others were left behind in the  hands of the taliban eight news nine  reporter victoria saha spoke to this man  exclusively she joins us from the  newsroom with more tonight victoria  imagine feeling absolutely helpless from  across the world wondering if your  family is dead or alive when you can't  get a hold of them in kabul this is the  daily fear this man is going through  knowing his family's fate now relies on  the taliban  in fear that the taliban may come across  this story this terrified husband just  wants to go by the name muhammad we are  hiding his face and altering his voice  so he isn't recognized there was just  like horrifying  just the stuff that go through your head  what could possibly  happen muhammad is spending many  sleepless nights making sure his  nine-month-old baby and wife are alive  sometimes he goes days without hearing  from them my stomach is like turning and  my stuff is going through my head and i  was like how come she's not responding  to my email  to my text he says when the u.s troops  were helping afghani families evacuate  his wife and baby were waiting in line  in front of the airport with hundreds of  other families desperate to flee before  the taliban took the reins of their  homeland  this is a picture his wife shared giving  you a glimpse of the conditions  basically it was three days and three  nights in the car  with no food  no water  no bathroom  with my nine-month  baby with her that was just one of her  six attempts muhammad says they had all  the necessary paperwork but was denied  when she got to the gate accused of  having fake documents by the taliban she  assumed that  the u.s gonna come through the gate and  get him out of the car and take him  inside  and that that didn't happen either  then she tried again this time she  almost lost her life they hold the gun  on her chest is you don't sit in your  car right now i'm gonna shoot you  and i don't care about you baby or you  muhammad has never met his baby and is  wondering if he will ever get the chance  to why is this happening to me you know  but i just prayed that everything goes  right  here have been in contact with our local  leaders senator jackie rosen's office is  aware of this situation they can't  comment on specific cases but her office  says in a statement in part quote  senator rosen will continue to provide  support and work with nevadans and the  state department on humanitarian efforts  in afghanistan and to assist americans  and afghan allies seeking to depart  reporting live from the newsroom  victoria saha 8 news now
 

